---
/**
 * K Culture Wire — **한국 그룹을 남·여·혼성으로 가른 지면.** (`/group-mix`)
 *
 * ── ⛔ 이 지면이 지키는 것 — 지우지 않는다 ──────────────────────────────────
 * ⛔ 「혼성이 12개」로 끝내지 않는다. **최소치**라고 말한다 —
 *    127개 그룹에 성별이 안 적힌 멤버가 있어 전원남/전원여 판정이 뒤집힐 수 있다
 * ⛔ 「왜 드문가」를 말하지 않는다 — 우리 자료에 까닭이 없다.
 *    업계 관행인지 기록 편향인지 우리는 못 가른다
 * ⛔ 밴드와 아이돌을 가르지 않는다 — 위키데이터가 한 속성으로 묶어 뒀고,
 *    우리가 가르면 그것은 우리 판정이 된다. 섞인 채로 내고 그렇게 적는다
 * ⛔ 성별이 하나도 안 적힌 49개는 세지 않는다. 0 으로도 남성으로도 밀지 않는다
 * ⛔ 수를 손으로 적지 않는다. 전부 `kcw-group-mix.json` 에서 읽는다
 */
import WikiTip from '../../layouts/WikiTip.astro';
import KcwRelatedArticles from '../../components/KcwRelatedArticles.astro';
import data from '../../data/kcw-group-mix.json';

const 수 = (v) => (v == null ? '—' : Number(v).toLocaleString('en-US'));
const c = data.counts;
const 혼성 = data.coed;

const TITLE = `Only ${c.coed} of ${data.classified} Korean groups have both men and women`;
const DESC =
  `Every one of the ${data.groups} Korean music groups on Wikidata, sorted by the sex recorded for `
  + `each member: ${c.men} all-men, ${c.women} all-women, ${c.coed} co-ed. `
  + `${c.coed} is a floor, not a total — ${data.couldFlipCount} groups still have members with no sex recorded.`;

const jsonLd = {
  '@context': 'https://schema.org',
  '@type': 'Dataset',
  name: TITLE,
  description: DESC,
  creator: { '@type': 'Organization', name: 'K Culture Wire' },
  isBasedOn: ['https://www.wikidata.org'],
  variableMeasured: ['group members', 'sex or gender as recorded'],
};
---

<WikiTip title={TITLE} description={DESC} jsonLd={jsonLd}
  canonical="https://www.kculturewire.com/group-mix">
  <h1>{TITLE}</h1>

  <p class="lead">
    Wikidata lists the members of {수(data.groups)} Korean music groups. For {수(data.classified)} of
    them at least one member has a sex recorded, so the group can be sorted. Of those,{' '}
    <b>{수(c.coed)}</b> have both men and women — {data.coedShareOfClassified}% — and the rest split
    almost evenly: {수(c.men)} all-men and {수(c.women)} all-women.
  </p>

  <p class="warn">
    <b>{수(c.coed)} is a floor, not a total.</b> {수(data.couldFlipCount)} of the groups we sorted still
    contain a member whose sex Wikidata does not record. Any one of those could turn out to be
    co-ed, which would move the count up but never down. We print the floor and the size of the
    gap rather than a single tidy number.
  </p>

  <section>
    <h2>The three buckets, and the {수(c.unknown)} we could not sort</h2>
    <div class="scroll-x">
      <table>
        <thead><tr><th>Group makeup</th><th>Groups</th><th>Share of sorted</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr><td class="nm">All men</td><td class="tot">{수(c.men)}</td><td>{Math.round(c.men / data.classified * 1000) / 10}%</td></tr>
          <tr><td class="nm">All women</td><td class="tot">{수(c.women)}</td><td>{Math.round(c.women / data.classified * 1000) / 10}%</td></tr>
          <tr class="edge"><td class="nm">Both men and women</td><td class="tot">{수(c.coed)}</td><td>{data.coedShareOfClassified}%</td></tr>
          <tr><td class="nm">No sex recorded for anyone</td><td>{수(c.unknown)}</td><td class="fine">not sorted</td></tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
    <p class="note">
      The last row is left out of every share above. A group with nothing recorded is not evidence
      of anything, so it is counted separately rather than folded into the men column.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>The {수(c.coed)} groups with both, largest first</h2>
    <div class="scroll-x">
      <table>
        <thead><tr><th>Group</th><th>Men</th><th>Women</th><th>Sex not recorded</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>
          {혼성.map((g) => (
            <tr>
              <td class="nm">{g.name}</td>
              <td class="tot">{수(g.men)}</td>
              <td class="tot">{수(g.women)}</td>
              <td class="fine">{g.sexNotRecorded ? 수(g.sexNotRecorded) : '—'}</td>
            </tr>
          ))}
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
    <p class="note">
      Ordered by how many members have a sex recorded, not by fame — we hold no measure of fame to
      order them by. Some of these are rock bands rather than idol groups; see below.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Where we refuse to give a number</h2>
    <p class="note">
      <b>We do not say why co-ed groups are rare.</b> Nothing in this data distinguishes an industry
      that makes few of them from an encyclopedia that records them less often. Both would produce
      the same table, and we cannot tell them apart, so we describe the table and stop.
    </p>
    <p class="note">
      <b>We do not separate bands from idol groups.</b> Wikidata files both under the same member
      property. Splitting them would mean us deciding what counts as an idol group, which is a
      judgement, not a reading — so the rows stay mixed and this note stays here.
    </p>
  </section>

  <KcwRelatedArticles page="/group-mix" />

  <section class="src">
    <h2>Where these numbers come from, and what they cannot answer</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><b>Wikidata (CC0)</b> — {data.source}</li>
      <li>
        <b>Members are people who <i>were</i> in the group.</b> The property does not separate current
        from former members, so a group that changed line-up is counted with everyone it ever had.
      </li>
      <li>
        <b>Sex here is what an editor recorded</b>, not a legal record, and it is missing for part of
        the roster. That gap is the {수(data.couldFlipCount)} groups above.
      </li>
      <li><b>Built {data.builtOn}.</b> A rebuild moves the counts as Wikidata is edited.</li>
    </ul>
    <p class="note">
      <a href="/group">Korean groups we track</a> ·{' '}
      <a href="/service-years">Group members by birth year</a> ·{' '}
      <a href="/about">How we count</a>
    </p>
  </section>
</WikiTip>
